From 33e8c7db6c5c3e3196900c8be1fe2e92e911ac65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:31:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2357/2409] media: v4l2-mem2mem: Don't leave the context
 aborted when STREAMOFF fails

v4l2_m2m_streamoff() cancels the job of the context before it asks vb2 to
stop the queue. v4l2_m2m_cancel_job() sets TRANS_ABORT, and only the
successful path clears the job flags again. If vb2_streamoff() fails, for
instance because the buffer type is not the type of the queue (an
OUTPUT/CAPTURE single-planar type on a multi-planar device), the error is
returned with TRANS_ABORT still set, and __v4l2_m2m_try_queue() refuses
to schedule the context from then on: every buffer queued afterwards
stays queued, no job is ever run and nothing is logged. A STREAMOFF of
both queues with the right types and a new STREAMON do not clear the
flag either, so the file handle stays unusable.

A VA-API driver that resets pooled decoder file handles by stopping all
four OUTPUT/CAPTURE buffer types ran into this on RK3588: the next decode
context on the handle (the AV1 decoder for 4K streams) queued requests
the hardware never saw and timed out waiting for them.

Reject a buffer type the queue does not have before touching the job
state, and clear TRANS_ABORT again (and reschedule the context, whose
queued job may have been dropped by the cancel) if vb2 refuses the call.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c
index a2a8748a63e8..c9dfed5b4c4b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c
@@ -1004,15 +1004,31 @@ int v4l2_m2m_streamoff(struct file *file, struct v4l2_m2m_ctx *m2m_ctx,
 	unsigned long flags_job, flags;
 	int ret;
 
+	q_ctx = get_queue_ctx(m2m_ctx, type);
+	m2m_dev = m2m_ctx->m2m_dev;
+
+	/*
+	 * v4l2_m2m_cancel_job() marks the context as aborted, and only a
+	 * successful STREAMOFF clears that again. Refuse a buffer type the
+	 * queue does not have before cancelling anything, and undo the abort
+	 * if vb2 refuses the call, or the context could never run a job again.
+	 */
+	if (type != q_ctx->q.type)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	/* wait until the current context is dequeued from job_queue */
 	v4l2_m2m_cancel_job(m2m_ctx);
 
-	q_ctx = get_queue_ctx(m2m_ctx, type);
 	ret = vb2_streamoff(&q_ctx->q, type);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&m2m_dev->job_spinlock, flags_job);
+		m2m_ctx->job_flags &= ~TRANS_ABORT;
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&m2m_dev->job_spinlock, flags_job);
+		/* A job cancelled from the queue above is still due. */
+		v4l2_m2m_try_schedule(m2m_ctx);
 		return ret;
+	}
 
-	m2m_dev = m2m_ctx->m2m_dev;
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&m2m_dev->job_spinlock, flags_job);
 	/* We should not be scheduled anymore, since we're dropping a queue. */
 	if (m2m_ctx->job_flags & TRANS_QUEUED)
-- 
